+#: CONTAINMENT, NOT A FIX. Q6_K dequantise returns non-deterministically wrong
+#: values on gfx1103 (Radeon 780M): eight runs on one fixed input tensor differ
+#: from each other, worst max|d| 5.8e-01 against the numpy reference, up to 75
+#: non-finite values in 262144, and it is wrong on the FIRST call in a fresh
+#: process, so it is not state accumulation. Q4_K and Q5_K are byte-identical
+#: across the same eight runs.
+#:
+#: The root cause is NOT established. Falsified by experiment, each separately:
+#:   -O3 miscompile (device-side -O1 rebuild: unchanged); HSA_OVERRIDE artefact
+#:   (a native gfx1103 build is worse -- Q5_K becomes affected too); a
+#:   64-thread-block hazard (a standalone HIP reproducer with 32/64/128 threads
+#:   writing disjoint half values is fully deterministic); unreliable GPU memory
+#:   (2 GiB memtest, 12 rounds, 0 mismatches across host-write, kernel-write and
+#:   kernel-verify); out-of-bounds read (4 KiB zeroed trailing pad: unchanged);
+#:   incomplete output coverage (sentinel-poisoned buffer: 0 of 262144 elements
+#:   left untouched); host ordering (explicit synchronize around every step);
+#:   launch concurrency (AMD_SERIALIZE_KERNEL=3); device->host readback
+#:   (GPU-side reduction agrees with the host copy run for run, and five
+#:   repeated host reads of one result are byte-identical).
